# English Code, Vietnamese Communication

## Codebase (English only)

All repository artifacts must be written in **English**:

- Source code, identifiers, and string literals shown in the UI
- Comments, JSDoc, and docstrings
- Commit messages, PR titles/descriptions, and README/docs in the repo
- Test names, error messages, logs, and config labels

Do not introduce Vietnamese (or other non-English text) into the codebase unless the user explicitly requests localized UI copy for a specific locale feature.

## User communication (Vietnamese)

When talking to the user:

- Explain findings, plans, summaries, and questions in **Vietnamese**
- Use Vietnamese for task breakdowns, trade-offs, and review feedback
- Keep code citations, paths, commands, and API names in their original English form

## Examples

```tsx
// BAD — Vietnamese UI string in code
<h2>Chọn mức cược</h2>

// GOOD
<h2>Select bet amount</h2>
```

```tsx
// BAD — Vietnamese comment
/** Danh sách spin đã kết thúc. */

// GOOD
/** Paginated list of finished spins. */
```

When the user asks for a plan: respond in Vietnamese; implement in English.
